{"name":"Deep Dive","hex":"#2e5467","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep dive","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of deep diving.","An in-depth examination or analysis of a topic. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative form of deep-dive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep_dive"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deep Dive (radio show)","blocks":[{"text":"Deep Dive is a Canadian radio program, which airs on CBC Radio One. Hosted by Rich Terfy, the program showcases famous record albums of various genres, which are played in their entirety with various anecdotes told between tracks."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_Dive_(radio_show)"},{"title":"Deep diving","blocks":[{"text":"Deep diving is underwater diving to a depth beyond the normal range accepted by the associated community. In some cases this is a prescribed limit established by an authority, while in others it is associated with a level of certification or training, and it may vary depending on whether the diving is recreational, technical or commercial. Nitrogen narcosis becomes a hazard below 30 metres (98 ft) and hypoxic breathing gas is required below 60 metres (200 ft) to lessen the risk of oxygen toxicity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Trevor_Jackson_returns_from_SS_Kyogle.jpg/330px-Trevor_Jackson_returns_from_SS_Kyogle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_diving"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG/500px-Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG/500px-Decompression_Dive-Preparation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u